WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.390
That was a great performance, Len-kun.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.100
As expected from Mr. Tsukimori's son.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.560
Not good enough. I need... I need to be better.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:58.090
A Peaceful Concerto

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:09.530
Or maybe... You're nervous because your parents are coming?

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.650
That's the first time I've seen him look so troubled.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.470
I didn't think he'd feel pressure from his parents...

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.740
Shimizu-kun?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.620
Watch out!

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:27.620
Ah.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.010
Don't "Ah" me!

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.480
It's a red light!

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.560
Hino-sempai... Good morning.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:38.520
He seems sort of out of it.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:41.230
You were reading and walking at the same time?

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:47.950
Yes. It's very difficult to do while I carry the cello.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.990
I wonder if there's a better way to do it.

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.860
Don't do that. You should just stop all together, since it's dangerous.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.990
Yeah.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.010
Why am I hiding?

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.960
Forget that, what should I do?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.610
I guess I can approach him all nonchalantly and say "Good morning"...

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.980
Good morning, Hino-chan!

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.660
Good morning, Tsukimori-kun.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.350
Oh, and sorry about yesterday.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:21.330
Hino-chan?

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.240
Maybe I shouldn't try and sneak up on him after all...

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.950
But, I should get this out of the way before the selection.

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:31.780
I should apologize directly to him as soon as possible.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:34.950
No, no. I should check on him discreetly first...

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.480
Hino-chan, what were you doing?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.440
U-Umm... Image training?

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:43.490
Huh?

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.160
Hey, where's Kaho-chan?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.390
She said she had to go do something.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.830
This is really bothering me.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.800
I won't be able to concentrate on practicing if I keep moping around like this.

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.270
Oh, Tsukimori-kun.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.480
Are you practicing during lunch as well?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.660
Yes. You too?

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:14.340
Yes, I need to finish my selection piece.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.570
How about you, Tsukimori? Are your preparations going well?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.190
Yes, more or less.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.700
It really is difficult with so little time to prepare.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.660
Agreed.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:31.000
This particular selection must be extra difficult for you, huh?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.180
There are some stupid people who are saying that, with your parents coming,

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:37.420
that you are going to receive special treatment.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:40.630
But I'm looking forward to the second selection.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:42.760
Even Tsuchiura-kun is participating.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:46.890
And I wonder if Hino-san will place higher this time.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:53.590
Well, you may not consider us rivals,

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.940
but let's each give it our all.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:31.490
It's selfish of me to not be able to concentrate on practice.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:35.800
I mean, Tsukimori-kun is under way more pressure than I am.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:40.910
If I don't give it my all, they're just going to eclipse me!

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.610
Tsuchiura-kun.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:51.280
What's this? You're practicing during lunch, too?

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:55.900
Or not, it seems.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:57.910
Yeah...

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.510
What's wrong? Something on your mind? It's not like you.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:03.300
It's nothing major.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.160
I mean, the selection is fast approaching,

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:10.550
so I was thinking about how I'd have to go out on the stage again...

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.000
I see.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:22.110
In that case, why don't you go practice someplace with lots of people?

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.200
Like a street corner or a park.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.030
What?!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.020
Don't act so scared.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:30.230
If you play in public, you'll keep your composure on stage.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:35.640
Oh, that. Yeah, I'll try that.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:39.540
Well, do your best. Though I shouldn't really say that right now.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.280
We're rivals now.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.970
Since I'm entering the competition, I don't plan on losing to anyone!

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:51.920
Though...

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.640
Let me know if anything is ever bothering you.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.900
Huh?

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.440
I'll gladly talk to you, as a fellow General Studies student.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.620
Thank you.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:11.380
But I can't depend on others forever.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.650
Not on Tsuchiura-kun and not on the magical violin.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.620
I need to do this by own my power.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.780
I have to practice every second possible.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.650
Shimizu-kun?!

00:07:33.650 --> 00:07:36.760
First it was Tsukimori-kun and now Shimizu-kun?!

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:43.550
Oh, he's just asleep.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.400
Now that I think of it, he was sleeping the first time I met him.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.960
Hino-sempai...

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:04.460
S-Sorry! I thought you had collapsed and...

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.730
Oh.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:09.650
Are you OK? Are you exhausted from practicing too much?

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.460
I'm always like this.

00:08:11.460 --> 00:08:12.230
Huh?

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:21.100
Sleep, wake up, play the cello, sleep.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.390
That's all I do.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:28.740
That's it? Surely you do other things, right? Like going out to have fun...

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:35.740
I go to concerts. And also the library.

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.340
The library? So you like books.

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:40.400
I do see you reading a lot.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:46.310
Yes, the library is a fountain of knowledge.

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:53.170
It's there that I learn a great deal about music.

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:58.130
Amazing. His entire world revolves around music.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:01.500
His mindset is totally different from mine.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:04.730
You really love the cello, don't you?

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:09.910
I suppose I do.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:16.730
He smiled! He looks like an angel!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.590
This isn't working at all. I must do better.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.390
Sorry to bother you during practice.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.910
The truth is, we came to cheer you on!

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.810
Look, we got refreshments, too!

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.430
Cookies, biscuits, and some desserts in cups for you to choose from.

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:51.810
This way your hands won't get sticky and mess up your practice.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:53.780
Even Mio thought it was a good idea.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.300
What do you mean by "even Mio"?!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.660
Thank you, Mio, Nao.

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.130
I gladly accept your offer.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.810
Isn't food not allowed in the practice rooms?

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.590
Just kidding.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:09.790
Mori-san!

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:11.770
Kaho?

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:16.670
Oh, she offered to be my accompanist: Manami Mori-san.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.370
I'm a second-year pianist in the Music Department.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:20.710
Nice to meet you.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:24.020
Looks like we still have some time.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:24.990
Huh?

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:28.640
Want to practice after we take a break up on the roof?

00:10:29.800 --> 00:10:35.780
Wow, I didn't think a girl in the Music Department would be interested in a General Studies student.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.310
I did my research on him already.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:40.100
He's on the soccer team,

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:42.040
Seems things are going well with her.

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:42.280
and he seems to be really popular.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.030
Yeah.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.850
I have people cheering me on.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.250
For their sakes as well, I have to work extra hard.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:16.540
I said I'd perform in public, but...

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:19.530
Maybe I'd feel safer in the park.

00:11:22.990 --> 00:11:26.730
Wow! What a lovely dress!

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:31.530
I wish Lili had that sort of fashion sense.

00:11:34.580 --> 00:11:36.810
Huh? Hino-san?

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:38.110
Amo-san...

00:11:38.110 --> 00:11:40.010
Wow, what a coincidence!

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.470
Up to something again today?

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.690
Umm, actually...

00:11:44.690 --> 00:11:48.970
This is bad. If Amo-san learned that I came to perform in public...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:53.420
Kahoko Hino caught doing special training in the park on her day off!

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:54.840
Seiso Times

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.690
Give me a break.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:00.880
Oh, are you shopping for an outfit for the second selection?

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:01.400
Huh?

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:04.150
If that's the case, I'll help you!

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:08.000
I may not look it, but I'm quite the fashion coordinator.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.820
Hold on, Amo-san!

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:12.560
Leave everything to me!

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:15.650
Oh, would you look at that. That's definitely...

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:19.700
I'm on fire today.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.480
Hey! Fuyuumi-san!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:29.770
Do you have a few minutes? How about you come help us pick out an outfit?

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.830
Fuyuumi-san! Can you hear me?

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.220
Hey!

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:42.240
Oh, that's nice.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.630
It looks reserved and ladylike.

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.450
Y-You think?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.210
I knew it!

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:54.090
With good fabric like that, the color is bound to look good.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.610
Th-Thank you very much.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.330
And here I thought I was going to practice...

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.440
I guess there's still time.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.430
Hey there.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.080
It's nice to see you again.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.590
Thanks for helping me last time.

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:23.230
Oh, it's nothing. You needn't be so polite.

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:25.750
Are you doing well with your practice?

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:29.220
Well, there's so much I still don't know.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.310
I see. Well I'll gladly help you if there's anything you need help with.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:34.490
Sure.

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.240
By the way, what's that?

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:38.860
Oh, this.

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:43.690
Actually, there's going to be a concert in the park hall.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.210
A concert?

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:53.030
An Invitation to a Piano Trio

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:48.770
There are some people who helped me out in the past who are involved with it.

00:14:48.770 --> 00:14:53.030
For that reason, I'm helping them out with the publicity.

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:55.820
Feel free to come.

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:56.870
Sure!

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:05.050
Here it is.

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:09.300
Shimizu-kun?

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.880
Hino-sempai...

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:20.280
The Schubert Piano Trio...

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.550
Three people are going to perform on violin, cello, and piano.

00:15:24.550 --> 00:15:30.910
They say all three are from famous orchestras.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:39.640
They do these shows on their own, even though they're retired.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:42.760
Wow, they're really impressive.

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:46.960
Oh, right. You said you often go to concerts, huh?

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:53.760
Yes. I try to go as often as I can, when I have time.

00:15:55.210 --> 00:16:01.750
Listening to other people play makes me think.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:05.900
About how my music is different from theirs...

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:10.890
About why they perform the way they do...

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:12.800
That's pretty deep.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:26.640
Wow, I feel so nervous.

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:29.360
You do?

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:32.940
Yes. It reminded me of the first selection.

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:36.310
I wonder if the nerves I felt up on stage came back to me.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.150
Is that so?

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:39.220
Huh?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:46.680
I feel something rather different up on that stage.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:48.070
Something different?

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:03.820
What is this I'm feeling?

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.290
It's different from the nerves I felt before.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.170
I feel like my chest is naturally becoming warm...

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:42.420
Wow, it's like the cello and the violin are having a conversation while they're played.

00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:47.470
And their two melodies are softly caressed together by the piano.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:56.770
I feel something rather different up on that stage.

00:17:56.770 --> 00:18:01.350
I get it. He really enjoys performing up on stage.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:05.550
That sentiment comes through in the notes he plays.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:12.330
Now I feel like all I've been doing is rushing frantically to try and play at a level

00:18:12.330 --> 00:18:14.570
as to not get left behind by the others.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:22.220
Making others enjoy the music... That's how I want to perform someday!

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:31.590
How was the concert? Did you have a good time?

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.250
Yes! It was incredible!

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:43.590
We are truly honored to have such a lovely lady grace us with her presence.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:48.720
No, I should thank you for putting on such a lovely performance!

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:51.730
Oh, do you play the violin as well?

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:54.750
Yes. Though I'm not very good yet.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:59.610
Oh, don't be modest. I love the way you play the violin.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:05.580
Oh, since everyone is here, how about you play for everyone?

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.540
Huh?

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.490
Yes, please do.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:12.650
Umm, it's really nothing special...

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:17.970
I would like to hear your rendition of Ave Maria.

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.110
Huh?

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:25.930
Come to think of it, the first piece I ever played on this violin was Ave Maria, wasn't it?

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:33.290
I heard Tsukimori-kun play it and thought that it could be quite fun to play it like him.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:38.570
All right. I will play you a song.

00:20:43.960 --> 00:20:48.400
I'm going to enjoy playing the violin and being in the competition.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.960
I'll give my all in the second selection!

00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:28.640
Seiso Academy School-wide Competition

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:45.990
I'm going to give it my all.

00:22:54.870 --> 00:22:57.350
Girls' Dressing Room

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:01.310
Hey, you're early.

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:03.540
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:05.850
What's going on?

00:23:05.850 --> 00:23:09.250
You look good no matter what you wear, huh?

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:11.380
Not so bad yourself.

00:23:13.630 --> 00:23:16.430
I'm sort of embarrassed to wear this outfit.

00:23:16.430 --> 00:23:19.170
Anyway, please go easy on me.

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:22.760
Oh, forgive me if something like in the first selection happens again.

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:24.870
Don't jinx me!

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:32.980
At that point, I had no clue as to the awful thing that was about to take place.

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:39.720
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:36.540 --> 00:23:39.710
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:40.320 --> 00:23:45.520
Schubert was a composer in the first half of the 19th century in Vienna.

00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:50.340
Since he wrote over six-hundred songs, they called him the "King of Songs".

00:23:50.340 --> 00:23:56.710
However, due to illness, he passed away at the young age of thirty-one!

00:23:56.710 --> 00:23:58.700
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:02.930
There's another famous composer buried in the grave next to Schubert's.

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:05.040
Whose is it, I wonder?

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:09.240
Next Episode

00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:07.950
The second selection finally begins!

00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:09.930
I'm getting a troubling premonition again!

00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:12.550
Umm, Hino-sempai...

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:15.500
I'm sorry, Shimizu-kun! There's no time!

00:24:15.500 --> 00:24:17.940
Next episode: The Aloof Virtuoso.

00:24:17.940 --> 00:24:20.050
Where'd he run off to?!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:21.810
The answer is...

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:25.050
Beethoven!
